I've been playing Nethack for maybe two months, but I am still unable
to succeed in the early game. Whatever I do, Nethack always finds a
way to kill my poor archeologist. Like yesterday: It was a promising
game; when I started there was dwarvish mithril-coat in the starting
room. Great. Then my almost first kill was hobbit with elven
mithril... Good. When I came to Gnomish Mines branch and saw the first
GM level is lit I proceeded to it. I killed hosts of gnomes and some
dwarves and hobbits. My AC rose to 0, my experience to 6 and I was
already skilled with pick-axe (and had telepathy, so blinding wouldn't
be such disaster like my previous game). After clearing the whole
first level I finally ran into a dwarf with mattock and killed him
easily. Things looked good, but my career was cut right there. My max
HP was at forties, with current HP being in twenties (the rest was
squandered by trying to kill off blue jelly holding all my daggers and
darts). Rabid rat approached, causing no alarm -- I've been hacking
these with pick-axe at basic skill without any trouble. So I started
it hitting with my new mattock. I dealt about six blows, most of them
(if not all) were reported as hits. After that I was dead. I was so
persuaded that I'm going to kill the rat with the next blow, that I
continued even as my HP got dangerously low and did not use any
evasive manoeuvres. What I don't understand how I managed not to kill
rather low-level monster with such a powerful weapon with good enough
skill. In my previous games when I got mattock, these lowly monsters
were dispatched with single blow and I could challenge even some more
powerful ones like mumaks. How come the damn rat could mount such a
successfull defense, I simply don't get it (and no, I did not die from
the rat's poison).


